[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4993954661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121292#issuecomment-4993954661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121292","id":4993954661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKamzZQ","user":{"login":"gilzoide","id":4603360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4603360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide","html_url":"https://github.com/gilzoide","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T15:57:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T15:57:13Z","body":"> However, you still need to set the syntax highlighter to Standard in the script editor manually in scripts opened with this PR, even if it's already set to Standard (otherwise, it will use the built-in Standard highlighting which doesn't work on Lua).\r\n\r\nYeah, that was a thing that I didn't touch: the syntax highlighter cached for scripts in `script_editor_cache.cfg`. Do you think this should be changed?\r\n\r\n> Out of curiosity, why doesn't https://github.com/gilzoide/lua-gdextension expose a Lua syntax highlighther instead of naming it Standard?\r\n\r\nActually, Lua GDExtension doesn't implement nor register any `EditorSyntaxHighlighter`. We have `LuaSyntaxHighlighter`, but it inherits from `CodeHighlighter` and is supposed to be used at runtime in `CodeEdit` nodes.\r\n\r\nLua script highlighting relies entirely in Godot's own `EditorStandardSyntaxHighlighter`. It always had this bug that you needed to open the script once, then close it and then reopen to get full syntax highlighting, but it had always worked (well, until 4.7 of course).\r\n\r\n`ScriptLanguage` has all these syntax-related virtual methods, I totally expect Godot to use them transparently, and it did work. (although by the way, I was a bit surprised that I had to create a custom ResourceFormatLoader for Lua scripts to work, in Godot 3/PluginScript it worked automatically).\r\n\r\n<hr/>\r\n\r\nOh, nice to know one can actually change the highlighter being used manually, I hadn't seen this menu item before 😅","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4993954661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5855622107","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121292#issuecomment-5855622107","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121292","id":5855622107,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXQWz2w","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/